---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' },
];

const lastReviewed = 'August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How this site handles data: no tracking scripts are active by default, the contact form doesn't store submissions, and what changes if that ever changes."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-faint">Last reviewed: {lastReviewed}</p>

      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        This policy explains what happens to information when you visit
        {siteConfig.siteName}. We've kept the site's technical footprint
        deliberately small: as published, this site does not run analytics,
        advertising or third-party tracking scripts of any kind.
      </p>

      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        Because no tracking or analytics scripts are active, we do not
        collect browsing behavior, device fingerprints, or usage analytics
        through this site. Your web host or hosting provider may still keep
        standard server-level logs (such as IP address and request
        timestamps) as part of normal infrastructure operation, independent
        of anything this site adds.
      </p>

      <h2>The Contact Form</h2>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> form opens your own email
        application with your message pre-filled, rather than submitting
        data to a server we control. That means the name, email address and
        message you enter are not stored, logged or transmitted by this
        website — they only leave your device if and when you actually send
        the resulting email yourself.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not set tracking or advertising cookies. If a
        strictly functional cookie is ever required (for example, to
        remember a display preference), it will be limited to that purpose
        and this policy will be updated to describe it.
      </p>

      <h2>No Sensitive Data, Ever</h2>
      <p>
        This website will never ask you to enter your Gold Rummy password,
        OTP, payment PIN, or other account-verification details. If you're
        ever asked for this information on a page claiming to be part of
        {siteConfig.siteName}, do not enter it, and please report it through
        our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>
        Pages on this site link to the Gold Rummy app and, occasionally, to
        other external resources. Those destinations operate under their
        own privacy practices, which we don't control and this policy
        doesn't cover.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This site is intended for adult users who meet the applicable legal
        age requirement for real-money gaming and is not directed at
        children. We do not knowingly collect information from minors.
      </p>

      <h2>If Analytics Are Added Later</h2>
      <p>
        Should this site ever add analytics or similar tooling, the
        integration will be added deliberately and disclosed here before it
        goes live, including what's measured and how to opt out where
        applicable — it will not be enabled silently.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the site evolves. Material changes will
        update the "last reviewed" date at the top of this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions can be sent through our
        <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
  }

  .text-sm.text-faint {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
